      "writtenOn": "2023-02-21T13:03:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From UEFI:\n\n\u003e If the size of the GUID Partition Entry Array is not an even multiple of the logical block size, then any space left over in the last logical block is Reserved\n\nso it should be skipped.\n\nFrom a Rust safety perspective, it doesn\u0027t change the fact that the primitive types that make up the `Entry` will have _some_ value (which is always valid for them).",
      "parentUuid": "88160037_79934fd5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 124,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 124,
        "endChar": 88
      },
      "revId": "26eda81d1b35eca0e6ed60832405f7ecb7a08cd5",
