      "writtenOn": "2023-02-21T13:03:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is like the difference between `memcmp` and `strcmp`: we know that the `name` slice ends at the terminating character so no need to parse `entry.name` beyond that.\n\nI\u0027m now comparing the whole array so any non-zero character past the 2-byte terminating character (which doesn\u0027t seem to be a well defined as `NULL` in C strings) will cause a mismatch.",
      "parentUuid": "0790418a_f80efb03",
      "range": {
