      "lineNbr": 172,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-21T18:00:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The `VirtIOBlk` instance is created by the iterator inside of the function so would go out of scope before the `Partition` does if that was the case.\n\nInstead, I\u0027ve given ownership of the `Partitions` to `Partition`, which we could extend in the future with `Partition::partitions(self) -\u003e Partitions` to rip out the object for re-use (if required); WDYT?\n\nThe part I don\u0027t like is that `Partitions::get_partition_by_name` now consumes `self` so that the `Partitions` instance is lost on error ... This isn\u0027t a big deal but doesn\u0027t give a clean API, IMO.",
      "parentUuid": "43251904_c18ab0e6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 172,
        "startChar": 56,
        "endLine": 172,
        "endChar": 77
      },
      "revId": "26eda81d1b35eca0e6ed60832405f7ecb7a08cd5",
