      "key": {
        "uuid": "e8391159_96bdb016",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/instance.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 172,
      "author": {
        "id": 1059815
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-23T00:24:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree with Jiyong that this is odd, and I don\u0027t think we should be optimizing for a hypothetical future that would anyway require refactoring.\n\nThe only user of `Partitions` is:\n```\nif let Ok(partitions) \u003d Partitions::new(device) {\n    match partitions.get_partition_by_name(\"vm-instance\") {\n```\n\nI would expect:\n```\nmatch Partition::get_by_name(device, \"vm-instance\") {\n```\n\nYou can even keep the function separation exactly as it is today (to aid potential future refactoring), just hide them inside the `Partition` struct.",
      "parentUuid": "e940805b_ea23b198",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 172,
        "startChar": 56,
        "endLine": 172,
        "endChar": 77
      },
      "revId": "26eda81d1b35eca0e6ed60832405f7ecb7a08cd5",
